  "slug": "machine-learning-assisted-83b8",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a proteomics paper package input validation and preprocessing as installable, reproducible steps upstream of analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is software that prepares data for downstream analysis. FastaGuard checks FASTA assemblies as a preflight gate and was tested on 700 NCBI assemblies and 1,040 injected faults. NBDC Data Tools assembles analysis-ready datasets from ABCD and HBCD releases in R and Python. gcat and its_a_scam provide C++ genomic coordinate handling and a modular single-cell toolkit for count matrix generation and per-cell quality control. WorkListGenerator structures proteomics metadata and block-randomizes LC-MS run order. DoAggregate sits at a different point in the workflow, performing rare-variant aggregation testing across genes, pathways and GO terms by combining 36 methods via Excalibur. What is new is breadth: several installable, reproducible steps now sit upstream of statistical inference rather than a single method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-08"
}
